# T002 warning: user code references builtin-if without a --- uses: header.
# Documents without --- uses: ["core"] cannot access raw builtin-* names directly.
# After T-828, the %libdir typecheck path uses the prelude TypeEnv as the baseline,
# so builtin-* names are not visible in user code that omits the --- uses: header.
# The type checker emits a T002 undefined-variable error for builtin-if.
# Eval succeeds because builtin-if is still present in the runtime environment.
[builtin-if true "yes" "no"]
=== out
"yes"
=== warn
undefined variable: builtin-if
